About the diamond systems:
The diamond systems themselves (LCL/corner, CLC, 3-6-9, Plus, etc.) are part of
the playing tradition of three-cushion billiards. This project documents the
author's formulation of them, corrects errata, and tests them against physics.
No claim is made about who invented each system.

Third-party code adapted:
- js/fisica.js, function chocarBanda: ball–cushion collision model of
  Han, I. (2005), "Dynamics in carom and three cushion billiards",
  J. Mech. Sci. Technol. 19(4), 976-984, doi:10.1007/bf02919180,
  ported to JavaScript from the implementation in Pooltool
  (pooltool/physics/resolve/ball_cushion/han_2005/model.py),
  Copyright (c) Evan Kiefl, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/ekiefl/pooltool
  (Kiefl, E. (2024). JOSS 9(101), 7301, doi:10.21105/joss.07301).
- Default carom table and ball parameters (table size, cushion height 37 mm,
  e_c = 0.85, f_c = 0.15, u_s = 0.2, u_r = 0.01, u_sp, e_b = 0.95) taken from
  Pooltool's BilliardTableSpecs and BILLIARD_GENERIC ball parameters.

